WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.480
When you work on the NCIS team, your life
is always on the line — and many beloved

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.660
characters have paid the ultimate price in
pursuit of justice.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.480
Let's take a look at what some of these actors
have been up to ever since their NCIS character

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.500
went kaput.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.100
Played by Sasha Alexander, former Secret Service
Agent Caitlin Todd was fiercely intelligent

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.000
and could easily craft detailed psychological
profiles of her suspects on the spot.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.920
She was smart, but not immortal: In season
2, she's caught off guard by a terrorist cell

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.780
in a warehouse and ultimately assassinated
by a sniper.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.239
This grisly development caught viewers completely
by surprise, especially since she'd already

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.040
been shot once during the episode.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:44.080
A bulletproof vest saved the day the first
time around, but alas, she wasn't so lucky

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:44.900
the second time.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:51.160
Since leaving NCIS, Alexander landed the plum
role of medical examiner Dr. Maura Isles on

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.540
another crime drama, Rizzoli &amp; Isles.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.370
She also had a recurring role on Shameless
as Helene Runyan, and has appeared in supporting

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.660
roles in films like Yes Man and He's Just
Not That Into You.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.560
Played by Alan Dale, former NCIS Director
Tom Morrow still felt a certain responsibility

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.640
towards his old team after retiring from the
job but that commitment ultimately cost him

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:13.320
his life.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.960
Still, he really knew his stuff just listen
to this:

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.200
"She worked at the Russian embassy in Turkey.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.840
The raid went pear-shaped and she was killed!

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.360
Not ideal, but mission accomplished."

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.160
"Meaning?"

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.870
In the Season 13 episode, "Return to Sender,"
Gibbs visits Morrow's home and finds him very

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:31.120
much dead in his office.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.930
We later find out he was killed by Trent Kort,
a former CIA operative who proved to be the

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.240
worst kind of traitor.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:42.840
Once Morrow's time on NCIS was up, Dale joined
the cast of the Dynasty reboot in 2007, playing

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.820
the role of Carrington family majordomo Joseph
Anders.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.600
"I know I'm going to regret asking, but what
exactly is going on?"

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.560
Dale got his start on the popular Australian
soap opera Neighbours beginning in 1985, and

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.540
made two subsequent guest appearances on the
show in 2018 and 2019.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.260
"Ah, you know, I have a real chance now with
Jane."

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.060
"AH.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.360
THE LOVELY JANE."

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.260
The death of Special Agent Michelle Lee was
a shocker.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.200
Played by actress Liza Lapira, Lee served
on the Major Case Response Team... and she

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.580
was hiding quite the secret.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.940
She was a mole who was constantly leaking
classified and sensitive information.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.120
When the truth is discovered, she confesses.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.680
Later on in the episode, Lee sacrifices herself
to stop her handler, Ted Bankstan, from escaping.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.140
He uses her as a human shield, and she gives
Gibbs the signal to shoot through her.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.780
Lapira has appeared in quite a few films since
leaving the show.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:40.400
She played Sophie Trinh in the 2009 film Fast
and Furious and memorably portrayed smart-alecy

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.020
Liz in Crazy, Stupid, Love.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:47.280
More recently, Lapira played Mia in the Netflix
series Unbelievable, based on the true story

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.220
of two female detectives investigating an
assault case.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:56.620
Played by Muse Watson, Michael Franks is the
man who mentored Gibbs and he was an invaluable

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.080
member of the NCIS team.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.620
Unfortunately, Franks wound up being brutally
stabbed by a serial killer outside of Gibbs

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.120
house.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.260
Watson is set to appear in the horror film
The Dead Ones, and he's landed a role on the

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:12.200
upcoming miniseries Diary of a Lunatic, a
follow-up to the film Diary of a Lunatic:

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.200
Trew’s Calling.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:19.660
In 2005, Lauren Holly joined the cast of NCIS
as Jenny Shepard, the new Director of NCIS.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.080
The character is subsequently killed off in
the Season 5 episode "Judgement Day: Part

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.810
1" after she's cornered by gun-toting assassins
in an abandoned diner.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:31.620
She doesn't survive the encounter… but at
least she proves to be exceedingly difficult

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.120
to kill.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:42.560
Following her exit from the show, Holly was
cast as Dr. Betty Rogers on the mystery series

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.740
Motive a stint that began in 2013 and ended
in 2016.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.060
She also plays the troubled Lynn Harper in
the third season of Designated Survivor.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:58.280
Played by Matt Jones, Ned Dorneget's time
with the NCIS team didn't last long, but he

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.760
was an integral part of the crew for several
seasons.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.260
The character died valiantly as he tried to
lead hotel guests to safety following a bomb

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:05.780
threat.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.320
Unfortunately, that threat wasn't an empty
one.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.580
Dorneget may no longer be with us, but Jones'
career is certainly alive and kicking.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:19.160
Since 2013, he's played the lovable bad boy
Baxter on the critically acclaimed series

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:19.660
Mom.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.680
It's safe to say this is much lighter fare
than NCIS.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.160
"You don't make a habit of burying money in
my backyard, do you?"

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.800
"I'm not really sure that's any of your business."

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:36.960
Jones is also featured in the wacky TV show
Let's Get Physical, and in 2019, he memorably

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.150
reprised his role as Badger in El Camino:
A Breaking Bad Movie.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:47.500
In March 2014, Lucas Black made his first
appearance as Special Agent Christopher LaSalle

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:48.700
on NCIS.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.910
Then in September of that year, he began his
long-running stint on the spin-off series

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.160
NCIS: New Orleans and quickly became a fan
favorite.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:01.180
But in Season 6, LaSalle was unceremoniously
shot while trying to avenge the death of his

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:01.680
brother.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:02.680
"Christopher…?

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.320
God, no!"

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.880
Some fans are worried that NCIS: New Orleans
won't feel like the same show without Black:

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.240
He was an absolutely essential part of the
series.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.180
Some viewers suspected he left because of
bad blood behind the scenes, but the truth

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.020
is actually far less dramatic than that.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.270
It sounds like Black just wants to spend more
time with his family.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:28.060
"There's a lot of priorities in my life that
get sacrificed for me to be here.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:31.419
But it's time for me to focus on those priorities."

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.620
As for what acting gigs are in his future,
we'll just have to wait and see.

